      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day, which is twice the 3200 mg/day maximum in the labeling. Single doses above 800 mg also add GI, renal, and cardiovascular risk without much added analgesia, and at 70 years old the patient is at higher risk for those effects.\n\nCould you confirm the intended dose? Some common options:\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **600 mg by mouth three or four times daily** (1800\u20132400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg by mouth every 6 hours** (1600 mg/day, typical for mild-to-moderate pain)\n\nIf 1600 mg four times daily is intentional, please confirm and I'll enter it, though I'd recommend checking with the prescriber or pharmacy first. Also let me know the indication and duration, and whether you want a note on the order, such as \"Elderly: monitor for GI bleeding and renal function.\""
      }
     ],
